 | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nTo determine whether $(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B)$ is logically equivalent to $A,$ we need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.\n\nWe see that the columns for $(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B)$ and $A$ are different. They differ in the second and third rows. Therefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B)≢A.\n$$" 13194139534126 17592186045417 true] [17592186411116 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411102 13194139534126 17592186045417 true] [17592186411116 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411108 13194139534126 17592186045417 true] [17592186411116 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411109 13194139534126 17592186045417 true] [17592186411116 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411110 13194139534126 17592186045417 true] [17592186411116 1069 "q-182422" 13194139534126 17592186045417 true] [17592186411116 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534126 17592186045417 true] [17592186411116 1071 "Find the missing values in the following truth table:" 13194139534126 17592186045417 true] [17592186411116 1072 #uuid "48976a89-8888-539a-bf0c-00c43763c6e1" 13194139534126 17592186045417 true] [17592186411116 1074 "First, let's add columns for $¬A$ and $¬B:$\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬A\\,$ | $\\,¬B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nThen, we add a column for the part of the expression that's in parentheses, $¬A∧¬B:$\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬A\\,$ | $\\,¬B\\,$ | $\\,¬A∧¬B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nFinally, we add a column for $B∨(¬A∧¬B):$\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬A\\,$ | $\\,¬B\\,$ | $\\,¬A∧¬B\\,$ | $\\,B∨(¬A∧¬B)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |" 13194139534126 17592186045417 true] [17592186411117 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411113 13194139534126 17592186045417 true] [17592186411117 1069 "q-127969" 13194139534126 17592186045417 true] [17592186411117 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534126 17592186045417 true] [17592186411117 1071 "Which of the following statements are logically equivalent?\n\n- $¬Q∧(P∨Q)$\n- $P∧¬Q$\n- $¬P∧¬Q$" 13194139534126 17592186045417 true] [17592186411117 1072 #uuid "b8076c0f-174e-5d1d-bedf-553b0bcc1d94" 13194139534126 17592186045417 true] [17592186411117 1074 "Two statements are logically equivalent if they have the same truth table. So, we construct a truth table for the three given statements:\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬Q∧(P∨Q)\\,$ | $\\,P∧¬Q\\,$ | $\\,¬P∧¬Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nWe see that only the statements $¬Q∧(P∨Q)$ and $P∧¬Q$ have the same truth table, so they are logically equivalent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139534126 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0150989f-9b6c-5f03-9a0b-cccc272d9946" 17592186411067 "answer-052a7912-8d7b-5fff-90e2-505d9e98c7